Foldcase (https://github.com/tao-io/foldcase)

## Lineage

Foldcase began as tao-io's fork of Openstory
(https://github.com/millionco/openstory), Copyright (c) millionco, licensed
under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

That fork incorporated the Foldkit framework adapter contributed by John
McAndrews (binarytide) in pull request millionco/openstory#4 ("feat: add Foldkit
framework adapter"), also provided under the MIT License.

The fork line — the Openstory core, the React shell, the CSF-3 catalog, and the
pnpm/turbo/vite toolchain — is preserved in this repository on the `foldkit`
branch, together with the feature branches that were open on it. It is history,
not a dependency of this line, and `main` no longer descends from it.

## This line

The `core` line is a new codebase: a Bun + Effect-4 CLI for Foldkit Showcases,
written by tao-io and licensed under the same MIT License. It carries the
Openstory copyright forward because it keeps two things derived from the fork:

- The **Showcase play contract** — a `play` thunk that throws on assertion
  failure — which is Openstory's boot play-runner contract.
- The **`SerializedError` shape** (`name` / `message` / `stack` / `code` /
  `docsUrl`), which mirrors Openstory's boot protocol so a Foldcase report and
  an Openstory `play-status` describe a failure the same way.

The original MIT copyright and permission notice in LICENSE is retained in
full. Modifications and new work in this repository are offered under the same
MIT License.
